7. Frontend updates the relevant state.
8. User Panel receives or fetches the updated published data.
9. A success or failure message is displayed accurately.

Do not rely exclusively on local frontend state for persistent changes.

Do not make the User Panel display an item as deleted when the backend operation has failed.

